# There are 10,500 fish&chip shops in the UK, serving 167 million meals a year (https://greatbritishfish.com/fish-and-chips)

# From a recipe online: ~200g of fish, 225g of potatoes, and ~50g of flour per meal
# This means 33,400 tonnes of fish, 37,575 tonnes of potatoes, and 8,350 tonnes of flour
# This is 3.18 tonnes of fish, 3.58t potatoes, and 0.795t flour per shop per year
# 410kg per crate of fish = 7.75 crates/shop/year, which comes out to 0.017 crates per Simutrans month
# Let's say a typical IRL fish and chip shop is 100 sqft -> 9.3 m^2
# The smallest Simutrans tile is 125mx125m -> 15,625 m^2
# Correction factor is therefore 1680
#
# 1680 * 0.017 = 28.56 crates/month of fish
# 28.56 * (225g potatoes /200g fish ) * (410kg per crate fish/700kg per crate vegetables) = 18.8 crates vegetables/month
# 28.56 * (50g flour / 200g fish) * (410kg/crate(fish) / 840kg/crate(flour)) = 3.5 crates of flour/month

Obj=factory
name=Fish-ChipShop1975
